      "body": "## What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nFix the generic torch fused forward path for FSDP2-managed LM heads,\r\nincluding models such as Qwen3.\r\n\r\nPreviously, the fused forward accessed `lm_head.weight` directly,\r\nbypassing the LM head's FSDP2 hooks and potentially mixing regular\r\nTensors with DTensors during matrix multiplication.\r\n\r\nThis change installs a fused LM head forward during backend initialization\r\nand runs fused computation through `self.lm_head(...)`. It preserves\r\ntorch/liger backend selection and handles DTensor weights, device placement,\r\nand hidden-state dtype inside the module boundary.\r\n\r\nThe Triton path is unchanged.\r\n",
